course: dictionary
lesson: 11335
title: Younger and the age difference
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Younger means having lived fewer years than someone else. If Maya is 9 and her brother is 6, Maya is older and her brother is younger. «My younger brother is six.»
explain: You can also use younger for an earlier part of your life, as in «when I was younger». The word comes from young, and its pattern is young, younger, youngest.
explain: When you compare two ages, you find the difference with subtraction. If A is 3 years younger than B, then A = B − 3. The question «How much younger?» asks you to find that difference.
fact: Younger means having lived fewer years than someone else.
fact: «Younger» is the comparative of «young»: young, younger, youngest.
fact: «A is D years younger than B» means A = B − D, so subtract the difference from the older age.
fact: «This year minus your birth year» gives your age after this year's birthday; before your birthday you are one year younger.
fact: If two ages add up to 20 and one child is 4 years older, the younger is (20 − 4) ÷ 2 = 8.
exercise: «Amy is 7 and Ben is 10.» Who is the younger? | Neither of them | Their mum | *Amy | Ben
exercise: «Sara is 12 years old. Tom is 3 years younger than Sara.» How old is Tom? | 15 | *9 | 7 | 12
exercise: Which word means having lived fewer years than someone else? | *younger | adult | older | ancient
test: «Mia is 11. Her younger sister is 4 years younger than Mia.» How old is the sister? | 4 | *7 | 15 | 6
test: Two children's ages add up to 20. The older is 4 years older than the younger. How old is the younger child? | *8 | 16 | 6 | 12
exam: Two friends' ages add up to 18. One is 2 years older than the other. How old is the younger friend? | 9 | 10 | 16 | *8
